{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017FUTX2oLSjMbTLGshqpt8B","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/source/highlighting.rst:10:Custom Highlighters\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:13:If the default highlighting doesn't fit your needs, you can define a custom highlighter. The easiest way to do this is to extend the :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` class which applies a style to any text matching a list of regular expressions.\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:18:    from rich.highlighter import RegexHighlighter\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:21:    class EmailHighlighter(RegexHighlighter):\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:43:While :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` is quite powerful, you can also extend its base class :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter` to implement a custom scheme for highlighting. It contains a single method :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter.highlight` which is passed the :class:`~rich.text.Text` to highlight.\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:53:    class RainbowHighlighter(Highlighter):"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bee08719-efa9-4731-880b-d7aaa00e6765","uuid":"fc9b1bba-c448-4081-a826-f4ccb1cf18bc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:08:30.184Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"docs/source/highlighting.rst:10:Custom Highlighters\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:13:If the default highlighting doesn't fit your needs, you can define a custom highlighter. The easiest way to do this is to extend the :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` class which applies a style to any text matching a list of regular expressions.\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:18:    from rich.highlighter import RegexHighlighter\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:21:    class EmailHighlighter(RegexHighlighter):\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:43:While :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` is quite powerful, you can also extend its base class :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter` to implement a custom scheme for highlighting. It contains a single method :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter.highlight` which is passed the :class:`~rich.text.Text` to highlight.\ndocs/source/highlighting.rst:53:    class RainbowHighlighter(Highlighter):","numLines":6,"totalLines":6},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017FUTX2oLSjMbTLGshqpt8B","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
